From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:40:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: pwm_bl: select the pinctrl sleep state while off

Some LED drivers only shut down once the PWM line is held low, and a
disabled PWM output may float or keep pulsing instead. Park the pin
through the device's sleep pinctrl state when the backlight is powered
off and restore the default state when it comes back on.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/pwm_bl.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/pinctrl/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
@@ -43,6 +44,8 @@
 	if (pb->enabled)
 		return;
 
+	pinctrl_pm_select_default_state(pb->dev);
+
 	if (pb->power_supply) {
 		err = regulator_enable(pb->power_supply);
 		if (err < 0)
@@ -69,6 +72,8 @@
 
 	if (pb->power_supply)
 		regulator_disable(pb->power_supply);
+
+	pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state(pb->dev);
 	pb->enabled = false;
 }
 
